From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:43:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Draw visuals into the buffers of captures of them.

Windows.Graphics.Capture captures a composition visual through
IWineCompositionVisualCapture, which a visual now offers: its size as
laid out, and a capture that, on every frame the compositor draws from
then on, draws the visual and what is in it into a buffer the capture's
sink gives, as a redirect visual draws its source, on the device the
capture is for, with a Direct2D context of its own.  The first frame is
queued at the start; with every buffer in use there is none.

The drawing is no longer tied to window targets: what a frame is drawn
with is the render's own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

